<entry>
<title>Across the sea, a ring</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/sundara-kanda/stories/ramayana-crossing-and-recognition/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/sundara-kanda/stories/ramayana-crossing-and-recognition/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/sundara-kanda/stories/ramayana-crossing-and-recognition/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T11:33:20Z</updated>
<category term="ramayana"/>
<summary>Hanuman leaps the ocean, escapes Surasa, enters Lanka and finds Sita in the Ashoka grove, giving her Rama's ring. From Valmiki's Sundara Kanda.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The day Lanka burned</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/sundara-kanda/stories/ramayana-lanka-ablaze/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/sundara-kanda/stories/ramayana-lanka-ablaze/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/sundara-kanda/stories/ramayana-lanka-ablaze/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T11:33:20Z</updated>
<category term="ramayana"/>
<summary>Hanuman wrecks Ravana's grove, lets Indrajit bind him, sets Lanka on fire with his tail and brings Sita's jewel to Rama. Lanka Dahan, from the Ramayana.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>Through fire to Ayodhya</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-home-and-responsibility/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-home-and-responsibility/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-home-and-responsibility/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T11:33:20Z</updated>
<category term="ramayana"/>
<summary>After Ravana's death, Sita's ordeal by fire, then the flying chariot carries Rama home to Ayodhya and to Bharata, who kept his sandals on the throne.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The fall of Lanka’s king</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-ravana/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-ravana/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-ravana/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T11:33:20Z</updated>
<category term="ramayana"/>
<summary>Nine heads given to the fire, Brahma’s boon, Mount Kailasa and the name Shiva gave him, and the king who would not give Sita back. From the Ramayana.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The bridge across the sea</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-the-bridge/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-the-bridge/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/yuddha-kanda/stories/ramayana-the-bridge/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T11:33:20Z</updated>
<category term="ramayana"/>
<summary>Vibhishana seeks refuge, Rama fasts three nights before the ocean, and Nala builds the bridge to Lanka in five days. The Ram Setu story from the Ramayana.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The unmoving star</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/krishna/books/bhagavata-purana/arcs/skandha-4/stories/dhruva-star/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/krishna/books/bhagavata-purana/arcs/skandha-4/stories/dhruva-star/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/krishna/books/bhagavata-purana/arcs/skandha-4/stories/dhruva-star/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T08:32:15Z</updated>
<category term="krishna"/>
<summary>Denied his father's lap at five, Dhruva goes to the forest and meditates until Vishnu appears and grants him the place of the pole star.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The deer, the vulture, the elder</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/aranya-kanda/stories/ramayana-loss-and-hospitality/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/aranya-kanda/stories/ramayana-loss-and-hospitality/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/aranya-kanda/stories/ramayana-loss-and-hospitality/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T08:32:15Z</updated>
<category term="ramayana"/>
<summary>The golden deer, Ravana carrying Sita away, Jatayu's last fight and Shabari's welcome: the Aranya Kanda of the Valmiki Ramayana, illustrated.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The bow that broke the sky</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/bala-kanda/stories/ramayana-beginnings/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/bala-kanda/stories/ramayana-beginnings/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/ramayana/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/bala-kanda/stories/ramayana-beginnings/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T08:32:15Z</updated>
<category term="ramayana"/>
<summary>Narada names the ideal man, Sita is found in a furrow, Vishvamitra teaches Rama, and in Mithila Shiva's bow breaks: Valmiki's Bala Kanda, illustrated.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The river in Shiva's hair</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/shiva/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/bala-kanda/stories/shiva-river/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/shiva/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/bala-kanda/stories/shiva-river/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/shiva/books/valmiki-ramayana/arcs/bala-kanda/stories/shiva-river/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T08:32:15Z</updated>
<category term="shiva"/>
<summary>King Bhagiratha's penance brings the river Ganga down from heaven; Shiva catches her in his matted hair. Ganga Avataran, from the Valmiki Ramayana.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>Hanuman Chalisa</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/hanuman-chalisa/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/hanuman-chalisa/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/hanuman-chalisa/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T08:32:15Z</updated>
<category term="hymn"/>
<summary>Tulsidas's Hanuman Chalisa in full: 2 opening dohas, 40 chaupais and the closing doha, with transliteration and an English meaning for every verse.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The Lion in the Pillar</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/krishna/books/bhagavata-purana/arcs/skandha-7/stories/prahlada-the-pillar/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/krishna/books/bhagavata-purana/arcs/skandha-7/stories/prahlada-the-pillar/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/krishna/books/bhagavata-purana/arcs/skandha-7/stories/prahlada-the-pillar/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T04:31:25Z</updated>
<category term="krishna"/>
<summary>Hiranyakashipu, who no creature can kill, asks his son Prahlad if his god is in the pillar; Narasimha steps out. From the Bhagavata Purana.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The bird, the thumb, the bow</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/adi-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-archers-eye/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/adi-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-archers-eye/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/adi-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-archers-eye/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T04:31:25Z</updated>
<category term="mahabharata"/>
<summary>Drona tests his pupils and Arjuna alone sees only the bird's head; Ekalavya, refused by Drona, gives his thumb as guru dakshina. From the Adi Parva.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>Flowers fell on Devavrata</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/adi-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-vow/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/adi-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-vow/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/adi-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-vow/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T04:31:25Z</updated>
<category term="mahabharata"/>
<summary>Shantanu loves Satyavati; to win her for his father, Devavrata vows to give up the throne and never marry, and becomes Bhishma. From the Adi Parva.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The song between two armies</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/bhishma-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-song/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/bhishma-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-song/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/bhishma-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-song/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T04:31:25Z</updated>
<category term="mahabharata"/>
<summary>At Kurukshetra, Arjuna lets his bow fall and Krishna, his charioteer, begins the Bhagavad Gita. Retold from the Bhishma Parva of the Mahabharata.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>Lo, I have won</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/sabha-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-dice-hall/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/sabha-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-dice-hall/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/sabha-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-dice-hall/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T04:31:25Z</updated>
<category term="mahabharata"/>
<summary>Yudhishthira loses everything to Shakuni's dice, Draupadi is dragged into the hall and her robe cannot be stripped. The Sabha Parva of the Mahabharata.</summary>
</entry>
<entry>
<title>The armour, still dripping</title>
<id>https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/vana-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-golden-armour/</id>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" href="https://spritual.co.in/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/vana-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-golden-armour/"/>
<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="hi" href="https://spritual.co.in/hi/collections/mahabharata/books/vyasa-mahabharata/arcs/vana-parva/stories/mahabharata-the-golden-armour/"/>
<updated>2026-11-13T04:31:25Z</updated>
<category term="mahabharata"/>
<summary>Surya warns Karna in a dream that Indra will ask for his armour and earrings; Karna, who never refuses, gives them. Kavach Kundal, from the Vana Parva.</summary>
</entry>
